  bootwright / render acquisitions
      List every artifact the selected desired state acquires or hands a Machine to acquire:
      the host packages and clients of the controller stage, each managed service's and the
      emulated BMC's image, each container cluster's release and declared mirrors, each storage
      cluster's images and package repository, and the installation media of the media store.
      Each row names the artifact, its version, its origin and that origin's class (vendor,
      public, declared, host repositories or media store), its SHA-256 and size where the build
      or the desired state pins them, the Machines that read it and the object that selects it.
      It reads the selected context's input, or with --input-dir a context-free input file or
      directory, registers nothing and contacts nothing.

  Usage
    bootwright render acquisitions [flags]

  Command flags
      --input-dir  Read a context-free input file or directory instead of a context

  Common flags
      --ascii       Use ASCII status markers
      --color       Select terminal colors (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --context     Select a context (default: current context)
      --detail      Select human detail (values: compact, full) · default compact
      -h, --help    Show help for this command
      -o, --output  Select output mode (values: text, json, yaml) · default text
      --progress    Select progress animation (values: auto, always, never) · default auto
      --width       Set presentation width (0: automatic) · default 0

  Examples
    bootwright render acquisitions --input-dir ./input
